## Phase 5 — General section/component scenarios
- Multi-column layouts collapse to one column (`grid` with `auto-fit`/`minmax`, or breakpoint changes).
- Navigation: collapse to a menu button; ensure keyboard and focus trapping in the mobile menu.
- Sidebars: become off-canvas drawers or move below content.
- Media: `img, video, iframe, svg { max-width: 100%; height: auto; }`; use `aspect-ratio` for embeds; `srcset`/`sizes` for images.
- Forms: inputs full-width on mobile, labels above fields, `font-size ≥ 1rem` on inputs (prevents iOS zoom), correct `inputmode`/`type`.
- Typography: fluid headings with `clamp()`; `overflow-wrap: break-word` on long headings.
- Fixed/sticky headers and footers: account for `env(safe-area-inset-*)` on notched devices.
- Hover-dependent UI: provide tap/focus alternatives; use `@media (hover: hover)` for hover-only styling.
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` for any added transitions.

---

## Phase 6 — Implement
- Change the smallest scope that fixes the problem; follow existing naming, file structure and conventions.
- Put shared fixes (e.g. a `.table-scroll` utility, a breakpoint mixin) where the project keeps shared styles, and reuse them across all affected tables.
- Don't break the desktop layout — responsive changes should be additive.
- Don't add a new dependency unless the user agrees.

---

## Phase 7 — Verify
Test at minimum: **320, 375, 414, 768, 1024, 1280, 1440, 1920px**, plus landscape phone and **200% browser zoom**.

Checklist:
- [ ] No page-level horizontal scroll: `document.documentElement.scrollWidth <= window.innerWidth` at every width.
- [ ] Every table column and cell value is reachable (scroll, expand, tooltip or stacked view).
- [ ] Sticky headers/columns stay aligned and have opaque backgrounds.
- [ ] Side padding around tables is reduced on small screens.
- [ ] Text is readable (no body text below ~0.8125rem), tap targets ≥ 44px.
- [ ] Works in RTL if the app supports it.
- [ ] Keyboard: scroll regions focusable, focus visible, no traps.
- [ ] No layout shift or regression on desktop.

If a browser tool is available, check the widths above visually and report any issue found.

